{"name":"Azshara Vein","hex":"#b13916","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vein","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blood vessel that transports blood from the capillaries back to the heart.","The entrails of a shrimp."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To mark with veins or a vein-like pattern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vein"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vein","blocks":[{"text":"A vein is a blood vessel in the circulatory system of humans and most other animals that carries blood towards the heart. Most veins carry deoxygenated blood from the tissues back to the heart; exceptions are those of the pulmonary and fetal circulations which carry oxygenated blood to the heart. In the systemic circulation, arteries carry oxygenated blood away from the heart, and veins return deoxygenated blood to the heart, in the deep veins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Vein_%28retouched%29.svg/330px-Vein_%28retouched%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vein","wikidata":"Q9609"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Figure_40_03_07.jpg/500px-Figure_40_03_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Figure_40_03_07.jpg/500px-Figure_40_03_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Layers of vein wall shown in comparison to arterial wall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigure_40_03_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg/500px-2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg/1280px-2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg?utm